{
  "_comment": "1.21.1 fabric mod-compat batch 01 of 4: Advanced Xray, Amecs, Better Statistics Screen, Chest Tracker, CobbleFurnies, ContainerSearcher, Controllable, Controlling. Same harness row as envs/1.21.1-fabric.json (uitest/1.21.1-fabric), so this file adds no Gradle row; the mods below are tagged \"harness\", so jt hands their pinned jars to that row as -PjechExtraJars and it loads them exactly as it loads jech/jei — every jar dev-classpath, because a standalone row stages nothing. Targets are authored as newest-release (describe.version \"\") and pinned by jt resolve. Cobblemon stays pinned but is not handed to the row: this loader remaps a mod jar at run time and never rewrites the Kotlin metadata, so its classes carry intermediary names into a Mojang-named runtime and it dies in its own initializer (Cobblemon's two targets are covered on the neoforge line). CobbleFurnies moved to envs/1.21.1-neoforge-mods-09.json: it hard-depends on cobblemon, which this env cannot load. Controllable is skipped as an upstream defect: its JEI mixin reads a field JEI 19.37 no longer has, the accessor fails, and JEI's whole ingredient overlay fails to build (see 1.21.1-skipped.json).",
